## 4. Test Products

The following products must be seeded with fixed UUIDs and the exact statuses shown:

| UUID | Title | Owner | Status | Price | Stock |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `11111111-aaaa-aaaa-aaaa-111111111111` | Test Active Product | Seller A | ACTIVE | 29.99 | 10 |
| `22222222-bbbb-bbbb-bbbb-222222222222` | Test Draft Product | Seller A | DRAFT | 15.00 | 5 |
| `33333333-cccc-cccc-cccc-333333333333` | Seller B Product | Seller B | ACTIVE | 9.99 | 3 |

**Why the DRAFT product?** The authorisation test `test_buyer_cannot_access_draft_product` (SR-AUTHZ-06) needs a product in DRAFT status that belongs to Seller A. A buyer requesting this product must receive a 403 or 404.

**Why a separate Seller B product?** The IDOR seller test needs a product that Seller A does not own, so the test can attempt a cross-seller modification.

---

## 5. Test Orders

The following orders must be seeded with fixed UUIDs:

| UUID | Buyer | Product | Status | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `44444444-dddd-dddd-dddd-444444444444` | Buyer A | Test Active Product | PENDING | Used for cancel and IDOR tests |
| `55555555-eeee-eeee-eeee-555555555555` | Buyer A | Test Active Product | DELIVERED | Used for review eligibility tests |
| `66666666-ffff-ffff-ffff-666666666666` | Buyer B | Seller B Product | PENDING | Used for cross-buyer IDOR test |

**Why a DELIVERED order?** The review tests (`test_buyer_cannot_review_without_purchase`, `test_buyer_cannot_leave_duplicate_review`) require a buyer to have a DELIVERED order for a specific product. Without this, the positive path for review creation cannot be tested at all.

**Why Buyer B's order?** The IDOR test `test_buyer_cannot_access_another_buyers_order` needs an order UUID that belongs to Buyer B, which Buyer A will attempt to access using their own valid token.

