## 8. Environment Variables

The following environment variables must be set before running tests. Use a `.env.test` file and load it in `conftest.py`.

| Variable | Example Value | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `TESTING` | `true` | Tells the app to use the test database |
| `TEST_DATABASE_URL` | `postgresql://user:pass@localhost/securemarket_test` | Test database connection string |
| `JWT_SECRET_KEY` | `test-secret-key-256-bits-minimum-length!!` | Must be at least 256 bits for SR-AUTH-06 |
| `JWT_ALGORITHM` | `HS256` | Signing algorithm |
| `ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES` | `15` | Must be ≤ 15 per SR-AUTH-05 |
| `REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS` | `7` | Per SR-AUTH-05 |
| `FILE_STORAGE_ROOT` | `/tmp/securemarket_test_uploads` | Isolated from development uploads |
| `MAX_IMAGE_SIZE_MB` | `10` | Per SR-INPUT-03 |

